{
  "name": "First Light",
  "type": "weapon",
  "img": "modules/dnd-players-handbook/assets/icons/items/longsword.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>A dawnbringer's blade, consecrated in a temple of Lathander at the hour of first light — its fuller inlaid with rose-gold that catches the faintest dawn.</em></p><p>In a righteous hand its edge kindles with the pale fire of morning, cutting not with steel but with light. A paladin of the Morninglord carried it east down the Trade Way and never came back, and a hobgoblin captain took it as a trophy, blind to the warmth still sleeping in the steel.</p><p>Once between dawns its bearer may call on the Morninglord's grace, and the blade's light pours into a single companion — a dawnfire courage that no fear can touch, steeling heart and body anew with every breath it burns.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
    "price": {
      "value": 2500,
      "denomination": "gp"
    },
